title: Gnomon voice works end to end; GUI re-pin, self-update and dictation shipped (2026-10-19)
summary: |-
  Voice was pulled forward from Move 4 and dogfooded the same night. Merged on feat/gnomon:
  - V0: voice allowlist, closed disarm reasons, the one-time clientApiId move.
  - V1: talk-only kernel principal.
  - Helper 1.6: arm custody, signed and notarized.
  - GUI re-pin: Claude binary re-pinned from a card with one Touch ID.
  - Self-update: build stamp, upgrade card, fd hand-over restart, one-Touch-ID resume; clientApiId moved again.
  - V2a/V2d: ambient ceiling, guards, mic pill.
  - V2b: GnomonVoiceIO.app, signed, with VPIO echo cancellation and hotkeys.
  - V2c/V2e: kernel-spawned client over a pre-authenticated fd, pinned to the build stamp; speakable replies; GUI enrolment.
  - Dictation: speech fills the composer; a countdown ring auto-sends; ⌃⌥H hold.
  Aegis reviewed every slice. Live proof in the log: the founder's enrolled voice turn was sent as voice, and Gnomon spoke the reply.
