decisions:
  - id: TD-2026-10-19-194
    decision: 'Voice slice plan V0-V9. Founder: voice turns under auto-edits behave like typed turns; signed single executable; talk-only fallback'
    rationale: The safest dogfoodable increment first
  - id: TD-2026-10-19-677
    decision: incident and daemon-stop are fully hand-only; reserve the disarm reasons and status.arms now
    rationale: A voice deny would cancel a brake the human started; closed lists before any client ships
  - id: TD-2026-10-19-063
    decision: Seamless re-pin and self-update in the GUI; move clientApiId so a restart costs one Touch ID
    rationale: 'Founder: terminal steps after an update are not seamless'
  - id: TD-2026-10-19-298
    decision: 'Ambient: no wake word; same as typed under auto-edits; Touch ID once per login'
    rationale: Founder wants natural hands-free voice; Aegis dissented, residual risk recorded
  - id: TD-2026-10-20-262
    decision: Dictation into the composer with a 5 s countdown ring, hold, and edit-holds
    rationale: 'Founder: review and batch before sending'
errors_encountered:
  - description: AVAudioEngine.start() failed with -10875 under voice processing whenever a player node was connected before start
    resolution: Attach the player after start, and ignore our own AVAudioEngineConfigurationChange while the engine is running (6fb6e536)
  - description: The client defaulted to push-to-talk, so an ambient attachment sat waiting for the talk key
    resolution: A new attachment's mode is the client's mode (5f591008)
  - description: The client read the attachment once at start; the Touch ID attach lands about 8 s later, so every utterance was dropped as not attached
    resolution: Re-read status every 1.5 s (c3565edb); the e2e test had masked it with a manual refresh
  - description: Update-watch compared distHash only, so a voice-only rebuild never offered a restart
    resolution: buildKey covers the GUI bundle and voice manifest (f4bb2d7e)
  - description: The GUI re-embed was missed after the clientApiId move (footer said clientApiId drift)
    resolution: Re-embed after every contract move
learnings:
  - Builders hit the 50-turn limit about a dozen times; the plugin release with maxTurns 100 is overdue.
  - 'Founder rule, extended: never hand the founder terminal steps after an update; the product restarts and re-pins itself.'
  - E2e tests that force a manual refresh hide lifecycle bugs; test the real timing (start before attach).
  - A disclaimed TCC child cannot launch from ~/Documents; install into a kernel-owned dir.
  - The pill under-reported failure (Listening while the client crash-looped); the founder only saw nothing happen.
